# License

`Wince-Docs` is a clean-room research and specification project. Its content
splits into two categories with different licenses:

| Scope | License | Text |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `docs/` — all specifications, policies, audits, appendices | **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)** | [`LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt) |
| `data/` and `tools/` — fact database, inventories, indexes, scripts | **MIT** | [`LICENSES/MIT.txt`](LICENSES/MIT.txt) |

`README.md` and this `LICENSE` file are covered by CC-BY-4.0.

Rationale, scope boundaries and attribution obligations (including for the
fact extractions from Microsoft documentation) are recorded in
[`docs/01-methodology/licensing.md`](docs/01-methodology/licensing.md).

Note on the fact database: `data/` contains *factual extractions*
(identifiers, numeric constants, function signatures, header/library
mappings) from publicly accessible Microsoft documentation, each record
carrying its source citation and retrieval date. Facts as such are not
copyrightable subject matter; the records are licensed MIT to make
machine consumption frictionless. Short attributed prose excerpts kept for
technical necessity remain the property of their respective owners and are
marked with their source in every record.
